LiveKit Egress exports LiveKit rooms and their media. It records or
streams a whole room laid out by a web template (room composite), an
arbitrary web page (web), a single participant, or individual audio and
video tracks, and writes MP4, OGG, WebM, MP3 or HLS files, RTMP or SRT
streams, WebSocket audio and JPEG thumbnails, to local disk or to S3,
Azure, Google Cloud, Alibaba or Oracle object storage.

It runs next to a LiveKit server and takes requests from it over Redis.
Track and participant egress use GStreamer pipelines; room composite and
web egress render the page in headless Chromium inside Xvfb and capture
its audio through PulseAudio.
